  "details": "Mic/\n\nStep 1:\nDownload Sonic Studio 3. \nSpecific version I'm using can be found here:\nhttps://www.asus.com/us/Motherboards/ROG-CROSSHAIR-VI-HERO/HelpDesk_Download/\nSelect Windows 10 64 bit, then select Audio, Show more \n\nDownload this \n\n\nVersion 6.0.1.8339 2018/02/27754.74 MBytes\n\nRealtek Audio Drive\nRealtek Audio Driver V6.0.1.8339\nUpdated Amplify Level behavior to prevent overwriting manual adjustments upon reboot or resume from sleep/hibernation\n\n\n\nThen in Sonic Studio, set Realtek as default audio.\n\nThen route VRChat to Vive headset.\n\nnow VRChat sound will come from Vive, but rest from speakers.\n\nIf you now go into game. The Vive will pick up mic sounds, but the mic wont get triggered. Leaving you muted. \n\nIf you go into Windows Sounds the mic is moving and activated, other software will still be able to use the Vive mic, but VRChat does not work with the mic.",
